WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.120
39% of glp-1 users reported nail detachment versus 9% of controls. This is Peptides Weekly, episode

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.640
6. Education and evidence, never-dosing advice. After that comparison, a surgery record, a

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:18.980
petition on unapproved peptides, a loophole fight, a mouse result, and this week's look

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:24.140
at research use products. Charles Taib's group brought a cross-sectional comparison, not

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:30.080
a randomized trial to the European Academy of Dermatology and Veneriology Congress 2026.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:39.060
Lab Roots reports that they compared 575 GLP-1 users with 1,329 people who had obesity or type-2

00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:45.140
diabetes and had never taken the drugs, drawn from France, the United States, Brazil, and Mexico.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:53.420
Discaleration showed up in 46% of users and 17% of controls, and any nail disorder in 66% versus

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.680
53%.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:01:00.040
Those gaps for detachment and discoloration stayed about two to three times as large, when

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:05.060
the analysts kept only people who had lost weight, and again after skin disease and nutritional

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:06.880
shortfalls were taken into account.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:12.600
The same people reported unusual hair loss at 50% versus 34%.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:20.060
Thinner hair at 42 versus 19, hair loss starting after treatment at 26 versus 12, and scalp redness

00:01:20.060 --> 00:01:24.140
about three times as often, often with itch, redness, or scaling.

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:29.940
Tayyip called the association clear and said not everything that happens on a GLP1 is

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:30.840
caused by the drug.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.740
About half the users said their nail trouble began before the medicine.

00:01:35.877 --> 00:01:41.657
Josephine Tolin, an anesthesiologist at McGovern Medical School at UT Health Houston, presented

00:01:41.657 --> 00:01:46.797
an observational record study on October 18th at the anesthesiology meeting in San Diego.

00:01:46.797 --> 00:01:52.557
Yahoo's account says the epic cosmos pull covered elective US operations from January

00:01:52.557 --> 00:01:59.457
2016 through December 2024 only cases longer than 60 minutes with at least a day in hospital.

00:02:00.037 --> 00:02:09.917
That pool held 2,8,601 patients and 145,610 of them about 7% were on a GLP1.

00:02:10.417 --> 00:02:16.477
After matching the users had 11% lower odds of a combined heart outcome and 8% lower odds

00:02:16.477 --> 00:02:18.057
of a combined infection outcome.

00:02:18.697 --> 00:02:22.337
The heart bucket mixed heart attacks, heart injury, strokes, and deaths.

00:02:22.857 --> 00:02:27.737
And the infection bucket mixed wound infection, urinary infection, pneumonia, and sepsis.

00:02:28.257 --> 00:02:30.757
So those odds do not belong to any single event.

00:02:31.817 --> 00:02:35.277
Emergencies, short cases, and same-day discharges were left out.

00:02:35.857 --> 00:02:45.677
A tighter match of 114,249 users, and 360,168 non-users, adjusted for diabetes and earlier

00:02:45.677 --> 00:02:55.317
opioid and NSAID use, put major heart complications at 1.0% versus 1.1%, and infections at 4.9 versus

00:02:55.317 --> 00:03:02.334
5.3%. The partnership for safe medicines filed a citizen petition on October 16, a regulatory

00:03:02.334 --> 00:03:08.274
request rather than a trial. It asks the Food and Drug Administration to block compounding by any

00:03:08.274 --> 00:03:18.314
route of seven unapproved peptides, BPC-157, KPV, TB-500, MOT-C, MEDEL-TIDE, SEMax,

00:03:18.674 --> 00:03:22.194
and Epitalon, and to set aside a July advisory vote.

00:03:22.694 --> 00:03:25.454
Agency scientists had recommended against all seven.

00:03:26.074 --> 00:03:30.434
The committee voted to allow six, and the petition says new members had financial ties

00:03:30.434 --> 00:03:34.274
to the peptide business, and that the meeting broke federal conflict rules.

00:03:34.274 --> 00:03:39.934
Examples Executive Director Shabir Imber Safdar said the scientists found no adequate characterization,

00:03:40.714 --> 00:03:44.354
extremely limited safety data, and no meaningful human evidence.

00:03:45.034 --> 00:03:48.974
Briefing papers said none of the seven had been adequately tested in human trials.

00:03:49.594 --> 00:03:55.974
The Alliance for Pharmacy compounding said in September 2026 that 503A pharmacies may not

00:03:55.974 --> 00:03:59.994
legally compound them now, and licensed pharmacies are selling them anyway.

00:03:59.994 --> 00:04:05.934
PSM bought several and four pharmacies in Texas and Pennsylvania compounded them and shipped

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:08.134
them to California within 45 days.

00:04:08.614 --> 00:04:13.714
The filing also says the FDA has reports of two deaths after illegally compounded Reda

00:04:13.714 --> 00:04:16.174
Trutide, a separate unapproved product.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:22.500
A bipartisan group of lawmakers is pressing the FDA to shut a loophole used to import knock-off

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:27.640
Reda Trutide, stat reported, and that push is a request, not new trial data.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:33.380
Retotrutide is an investigational obesity drug from Eli Lilly, so a knock-off import

00:04:33.380 --> 00:04:34.800
is not an approved medicine.

00:04:35.961 --> 00:04:41.441
Semiglutide and Tedu-glutide reduced immune-driven gut injury and mice, news medical reported,

00:04:41.721 --> 00:04:43.661
and a mouse result is not a human result.

00:04:44.341 --> 00:04:49.901
Semiglutide is a GLP1 receptor agonist, and this animal finding does not create a new human

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:50.161
use.

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:57.635
Away from the drug studies, TikTok is blocking peptide searches, EEW magazine reports, hospitals

00:04:57.635 --> 00:05:02.975
in New South Wales are seeing a surge in peptide-related presentations, the New England Times reports.

00:05:04.226 --> 00:05:07.686
Peptide Semiglutide sold without a prescription is this week's spotlight,

00:05:08.146 --> 00:05:12.586
and a public health reports paper says a legal loophole lets people buy it while the selling

00:05:12.586 --> 00:05:18.486
sites skip both the supplies and the guidance. That label is a sales description. It is not a

00:05:18.486 --> 00:05:23.346
regulator's finding that anyone checked identity, strength, sterility, or a human benefit.

00:05:23.346 --> 00:05:34.566
From September 1, 2025 through January 30, 2026, the team watched college students at the University of Connecticut and older adults try the preparation after searching online.

00:05:35.226 --> 00:05:46.586
20 adults took part, 12 men and 8 women, mean age 40, with a wide age spread. They were handed semi-glutide vials, diluent and supplies, and scored on 34 steps.

00:05:46.586 --> 00:05:51.306
This was not a treatment study, weight, glucose, and symptoms were not the outcome.

00:05:51.786 --> 00:05:55.706
Completing the steps was, they got 15 of the 34 steps right.

00:05:56.246 --> 00:06:02.206
The average score was 44%, and the spread around that average was 50%age points, so some

00:06:02.206 --> 00:06:04.526
people managed far more of the sequence than others.

00:06:05.046 --> 00:06:08.666
The mistakes lined up with a wrong dose, a needle stick, or an infection.

00:06:09.266 --> 00:06:14.406
Confidence sat at 2.3 out of 5 before the demonstration, and 1.9 after it.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:17.066
That dip was not statistically significant.

00:06:17.446 --> 00:06:20.346
People were unsure at the start and still unsure at the end.

00:06:20.806 --> 00:06:22.226
And most steps were still missed.

00:06:22.786 --> 00:06:27.346
The authors say untrained adults with no experience in injecting medicines could face a high risk

00:06:27.346 --> 00:06:32.366
of harm if they tried a self-administered gray market peptide semi-glutide from internet instructions

00:06:32.366 --> 00:06:32.726
alone.

00:06:33.386 --> 00:06:38.166
They also want a larger, more mixed group and the same test on other peptides sold without

00:06:38.166 --> 00:06:38.746
a prescription.

00:06:39.406 --> 00:06:41.406
Twenty people do not map the whole market.

00:06:41.406 --> 00:06:47.446
A 2026 narrative review in curious widens the frame, and it is not a trial and it enrolled

00:06:47.446 --> 00:06:48.006
nobody.

00:06:48.386 --> 00:06:53.126
It calls unregulated peptide use a public health problem carried by digital promotion.

00:06:53.726 --> 00:06:58.386
It also says peptide medicines have real roles when they are developed, prescribed, made,

00:06:58.666 --> 00:07:00.206
and watched through regulated paths.

00:07:00.786 --> 00:07:06.566
The promotion it describes aims experimental or weekly evidence peptides at fat loss, recovery,

00:07:07.046 --> 00:07:09.986
looks, cognition, performance, and longevity.

00:07:09.986 --> 00:07:22.606
The chain it traces runs through online promotion, gray market access, self injection, stacking, informal titration, uncertain product quality, muddy rules, and weak adverse event tracking.

00:07:23.226 --> 00:07:27.006
Stacking in that account means using more than one of these products together.

00:07:27.626 --> 00:07:30.746
Informal titration means changing the amount without a clinician.

00:07:31.466 --> 00:07:34.246
Those are descriptions of the sales culture, not a method.

00:07:34.806 --> 00:07:37.586
The review's worry is not legitimate peptide medicine.

00:07:37.586 --> 00:07:44.286
It is people experimenting with products whose identity, purity, potency, sterility, and safety are uncertain.

00:07:44.946 --> 00:07:49.786
A label can name a peptide while the vials' contents, strength, and cleanliness stay unknown.

00:07:50.466 --> 00:07:54.466
The review did not test a product, so it establishes no contamination rate.

00:07:54.986 --> 00:08:02.106
What it does establish as a narrative review is that those uncertainties sit on the same path as home injection and thin safety reporting.

00:08:02.746 --> 00:08:07.726
Regulated therapy in these sources is the path of development, prescription, manufacture,

00:08:08.126 --> 00:08:08.686
and monitoring.

00:08:09.366 --> 00:08:13.866
A loophole purchase of peptide semaglutide is not an approval to prepare and inject it

00:08:13.866 --> 00:08:14.286
at home.

00:08:14.886 --> 00:08:19.946
Neither paper shows that gray market peptides cause fat loss, faster healing, clearer thinking,

00:08:20.266 --> 00:08:21.066
or longer life.

00:08:21.626 --> 00:08:25.566
The 20-person exercise measured steps and confidence, not a health outcome.

00:08:26.186 --> 00:08:29.746
A low score speaks to handling risk, not to whether the peptide works.

00:08:29.746 --> 00:08:34.746
The review does not count how often products are mislabeled or harmful. It's

00:08:34.746 --> 00:08:39.746
called for clinician awareness, adverse event reporting, quality checks, clearer digital

00:08:39.746 --> 00:08:44.526
warnings, and proportionate oversight is a recommendation. Not proof those safeguards

00:08:44.526 --> 00:08:49.790
already work. One thing worth knowing is that a cross-sectional Congress comparison can

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:56.030
tie GLP1 use to more nail and hair complaints without showing the drugs cause them. Also worth

00:08:56.030 --> 00:09:01.170
knowing, a surgical record analysis can link GLP1 use to slightly lower odds of combined

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:03.810
heart and infection trouble after planned surgery.

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:08.590
And that small gap in match charts is not proof the drug's protective person heading

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:09.410
to an operation.

00:09:10.070 --> 00:09:15.210
And a small observed test can show untrained adults missing most steps with gray market peptide

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:20.710
semi-glutide, which is a handling risk outside a prescription pathway, not evidence those

00:09:20.710 --> 00:09:21.850
products treat anything.

